{"name":"Starfish","hex":"#e5bca5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"starfish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various echinoderms (not in fact fish) with usually five arms, many of which eat bivalves or corals by everting their stomach.","Any many-armed or tentacled sea invertebrate, whether cnidarian, echinoderm, or cephalopod."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To assume a splayed-out shape, like that of a starfish.\n\nWhile floating on water","While floating on water"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starfish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Starfish","blocks":[{"text":"Starfish or sea stars are a class of echinoderms generally shaped like a star polygon. Starfish are also known as asteroids because they form the taxonomic class Asteroidea. About 1,900 species of starfish live on the seabed, and are found in all the world's oceans, from warm, tropical zones to frigid, polar regions. They can occur from the intertidal zone down to abyssal depths, at 6,000 m (20,000 ft) below the surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Starfish_montage.png/330px-Starfish_montage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starfish","wikidata":"Q25349"},{"title":"Starfish (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Starfish is the fifth album by the Australian rock band The Church, released in February 1988 by Mushroom Records in Australia and by Arista Records internationally. The band's international breakthrough album, Starfish went gold in America and has remained their most commercially successful release. The album sold 600,000 copies in the United States alone. The first single, \"Under the Milky Way\", charted on the US Billboard Hot 100, peaking at No. 24, and at No. 2 on the Mainstream Rock Tracks chart, leading to significant exposure of the then relatively underground Australian act. In Australia \"Under the Milky Way\" climbed to No. 22, and Starfish reached No. 11 on the albums chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/66/Starfish_album.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starfish_(album)","wikidata":"Q3968358"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Luidia_maculata%2C_Ras_Sedr%2C_Egypt.jpg/330px-Luidia_maculata%2C_Ras_Sedr%2C_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Luidia_maculata%2C_Ras_Sedr%2C_Egypt.jpg/960px-Luidia_maculata%2C_Ras_Sedr%2C_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Luidia_maculata%2C_Ras_Sedr%2C_Egypt.jpg/330px-Luidia_maculata%2C_Ras_Sedr%2C_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALuidia_maculata%2C_Ras_Sedr%2C_Egypt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Astropecten_aranciacus_Naxos08_1775_dett.jpg/330px-Astropecten_aranciacus_Naxos08_1775_dett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/Astropecten_aranciacus_Naxos08_1775_dett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Astropecten_aranciacus_Naxos08_1775_dett.jpg/330px-Astropecten_aranciacus_Naxos08_1775_dett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAstropecten_aranciacus_Naxos08_1775_dett.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/P%C3%A9dicellaires_d%27_Acanthaster_Planci.JPG/330px-P%C3%A9dicellaires_d%27_Acanthaster_Planci.JPG?utm_source=en.